1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,929
Yeah. Um, I mean, it's whatever works for you, I guess.

2
00:00:10,529 --> 00:00:13,314
Three things killed our first business.

3
00:00:13,314 --> 00:00:18,671
The first was pricing. We charged eighty dollars an hour for eleven months.

4
00:00:18,671 --> 00:00:23,529
Our rent alone was four thousand a month, so the maths never closed.

5
00:00:23,529 --> 00:00:26,743
Why did it take us eleven months to see that?

6
00:00:26,743 --> 00:00:31,386
Because we were measuring revenue and never once measured margin.

7
00:00:31,386 --> 00:00:36,529
The second was Tuesday meetings. Ninety minutes, every week, for a year.

8
00:00:36,529 --> 00:00:40,743
Turns out a meeting with no owner is just a nicer argument.

9
00:00:40,743 --> 00:00:46,457
The third was hiring. We took on two people in March before the revenue existed.

10
00:00:46,457 --> 00:00:51,814
If you are reading your own numbers once a quarter, you are already behind.

11
00:00:51,814 --> 00:00:56,814
We closed it in June. It cost sixty thousand dollars and a friendship.

12
00:00:56,814 --> 00:01:01,743
I would price differently tomorrow. The hiring I would simply not do.

13
00:01:04,343 --> 00:01:08,271
Yeah. Um, I mean, it's whatever works for you, I guess.

14
00:01:08,271 --> 00:01:11,414
Right, right. And stuff like that, you know.

15
00:01:11,414 --> 00:01:13,614
Totally. Yeah, no, for sure.

16
00:01:16,214 --> 00:01:19,714
So what was the moment you knew it had to change?

17
00:01:19,714 --> 00:01:24,500
It was a Thursday in April. We had forty-one clients and no system.

18
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:30,143
I was answering the same question twelve times a day, from my phone, at dinner.

19
00:01:30,143 --> 00:01:36,143
My daughter asked me to put it down and I said one minute, and it was not one minute.

20
00:01:36,143 --> 00:01:41,143
That was the moment. Not the revenue, not the burnout, the one minute.

21
00:01:41,143 --> 00:01:46,714
Turns out the business was fine. I was the bottleneck and I built it that way.

22
00:01:46,714 --> 00:01:51,643
We wrote down every repeated question and answered it once, properly.

23
00:01:51,643 --> 00:01:56,143
Within three weeks I was fielding four a day instead of twelve.

24
00:01:56,143 --> 00:02:01,429
If you are the only door into your own company, you do not have a company.

25
00:02:01,429 --> 00:02:06,429
The work did not shrink. I just stopped being the only way through it.

26
00:02:08,829 --> 00:02:12,757
Yeah. Um, I mean, it's whatever works for you, I guess.
